WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.074
Threat hunters rely on many sources of information.

2
00:00:03.074 --> 00:00:17.491
These may include EDR telemetry, SIEM logs, authentication events, DNS activity, firewall records, cloud logs, proxy logs, endpoint artifacts, network telemetry, and threat intelligence.

3
00:00:17.491 --> 00:00:22.530
The quality of a hunt often depends on the quality and completeness of available data.

4
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.284
Missing visibility creates blind spots.

5
00:00:25.284 --> 00:00:32.657
A hypothesis cannot be tested reliably if the organization does not collect the telemetry needed to observe the behavior.

6
00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:34.104
Context also matters.

7
00:00:34.104 --> 00:00:37.766
An unusual process on one system may be normal on another.

8
00:00:37.766 --> 00:00:45.210
A login pattern may be expected for one role but suspicious for a different user, location, time, or system.

9
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:50.189
Hunters combine technical evidence with environmental knowledge to make informed judgments.

10
00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:58.919
They look for patterns, timelines, relationships, and exceptions that help distinguish normal operations from activity that needs further investigation.
